{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-bad-hop/audio/main-d745cbb8128c.mp3","durationSec":124.152,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.34,"text":"BAD HOP were a hip-hop crew of eight rappers from Kawasaki."},{"start":4.3,"end":6.26,"text":"A crew is a group of people who work together."},{"start":7.22,"end":9.3,"text":"Rappers speak words with the beat of the music."},{"start":10.06,"end":11.9,"text":"They started the group in 2014."},{"start":12.84,"end":15.58,"text":"They were friends long before they became a music group."},{"start":16.44,"end":20.06,"text":"Twin brothers T-Pablow and YZERR were at the centre of the group."},{"start":20.06,"end":24.4,"text":"Twins are two children born to the same mother at the same time."},{"start":25.2,"end":27.78,"text":"The brothers helped lead the crew and make its music."},{"start":28.42,"end":30.94,"text":"The friends grew up in a difficult part of Kawasaki."},{"start":31.7,"end":33.26,"text":"Money was a problem in their area."},{"start":33.26,"end":36.26,"text":"Rap gave them a way to tell people about their lives."},{"start":36.26,"end":39.34,"text":"T-Pablow started rapping as a teenager."},{"start":39.9,"end":42.94,"text":"In 2012, he won the BAZOOKA!!!"},{"start":44.5,"end":46.3,"text":"High School Rap Championship."},{"start":47.74,"end":50.24,"text":"It was a rap battle contest for young rappers."},{"start":50.92,"end":54.44,"text":"In a rap battle, people take turns rapping against each other."},{"start":54.86,"end":56.66,"text":"They make up their words as they rap."},{"start":57.26,"end":59.52,"text":"The words are not from a song they learned before."},{"start":59.52,"end":64.18,"text":"BAD HOP worked independently, without a big record company behind them."},{"start":64.7,"end":68.74,"text":"Here, independent means doing the work and making the decisions yourself."},{"start":69.34,"end":70.84,"text":"They had to do more than write songs."},{"start":72.46,"end":76.38,"text":"In 2018, they gave a concert at Nippon Budokan in Tokyo."},{"start":77.08,"end":80.6,"text":"A concert is a show where people perform music for other people."},{"start":81.24,"end":82.36,"text":"All the tickets sold."},{"start":82.88,"end":86.08,"text":"They organised the concert themselves and paid its costs."},{"start":86.86,"end":89.24,"text":"That meant finding the money to put the show on."},{"start":89.8,"end":92.32,"text":"Their work included the business side of music."},{"start":92.32,"end":97.72,"text":"BAD HOP gave their final concert at Tokyo Dome in February 2024."},{"start":98.76,"end":103.3,"text":"They were the first Japanese hip-hop group to headline their own concert there."},{"start":103.98,"end":106.46,"text":"Headline means being the main act at a show."},{"start":107.34,"end":108.76,"text":"The group ended after that night."},{"start":109.32,"end":112.22,"text":"Fans heard old songs and new music during the concert."},{"start":112.96,"end":116.14,"text":"The music brought parts of their story together in one show."},{"start":117.18,"end":120.2,"text":"Later, YZERR released new music under his own name."},{"start":120.6,"end":123.6,"text":"He continued his story as a rapper after the group ended."}],"words":[{"text":"BAD","start":0,"end":0.25},{"text":"HOP","start":0.25,"end":0.5},{"text":"were","start":0.5,"end":0.88},{"text":"a","start":0.88,"end":1.02},{"text":"hip-hop","start":1.02,"end":1.38},{"text":"crew","start":1.38,"end":1.64},{"text":"of","start":1.64,"end":1.82},{"text":"eight","start":1.82,"end":2.06},{"text":"rappers","start":2.06,"end":2.46},{"text":"from","start":2.46,"end":2.76},{"text":"Kawasaki","start":2.76,"end":3.34},{"text":"A","start":4.3,"end":4.32},{"text":"crew","start":4.32,"end":4.58},{"text":"is","start":4.58,"end":4.72},{"text":"a","start":4.72,"end":4.84},{"text":"group","start":4.84,"end":4.98},{"text":"of","start":4.98,"end":5.16},{"text":"people","start":5.16,"end":5.42},{"text":"who","start":5.42,"end":5.62},{"te